***REMOVED***"details": "<p>Welcome to the <strong style=\"background-color: initial\">Faculty of Business and Law!<\/strong><\/p><p>This orientation session is for students commencing in <strong>Bachelor of Property Economics <\/strong>and associated double degrees.<\/p><p>Please join us initially for a catered light <strong>Lunch on the Lawn<\/strong> and an opportunity to visit our Student Club stalls before commencing your Property Economics information session and Connect 101.<\/p><p><strong><em>Logistics<\/em><\/strong><em>:<\/em><\/p><p>Meet at <strong>Gardens Point - P Block - room P-514 @ 12.15pm prompt<\/strong>, for registration and a lunch identification for collection. (<em>NB: if you are attending the 'optional workshop' in the morning you won't need to register until 1.30pm)<\/em><\/p><p><strong>12.30 \u2013 1.30pm:<\/strong> Lunch on the Lawn<\/p><p>Join us for a catered, light Lunch on the Kidney Lawn*<\/p><ul>***REMOVED***   <li>Mingle***REMOVED***   with staff and peers<\/li>   <li>Visit***REMOVED***   the various Student Club stalls on the Lawn<\/li> <\/ul><p>* <em>Whilst we will have a variety of lunch boxes to cater for some dietary needs, if you have detailed requirements, you may prefer to bring your own lunch or purchase from the retailers on campus.<\/em><\/p><p><em><br> <strong>1.30-3.00pm<\/strong>: Return to P-514 for your Property Economics Information session:<\/em><\/p><ul>***REMOVED******REMOVED***<li>30***REMOVED***minutes of welcome including an interactive discussion panel (<em>current***REMOVED***property students and recent graduates<\/em><strong>)<\/strong><\/li>***REMOVED***<li>60***REMOVED***minutes of networking and property related in-class activities<\/li>  <\/ul><p><strong>3.00-4.30pm:<\/strong> Connect 101<\/p><ul>***REMOVED******REMOVED***<li>Volunteer***REMOVED***students will provide you with a \"101\" of all things QUT,***REMOVED***including support services, IT, and the student experience outside the***REMOVED***classroom.<\/li>***REMOVED***<li>Further***REMOVED***opportunity to socialise with peers in your course and ask questions.<\/li>  <\/ul><p>If you are studying a double degree, you will also be required to attend the orientation session for the other part of your double degree, which may be on a different day.<\/p><p>This is an in-person orientation session including catering. Please make sure you register if you plan to attend - or cancel in a timely manner if your plans need to change!<\/p><p>An online version of this session is available. If you would prefer attending online or are unable to make it to campus, please register for the <strong>online<\/strong> version of this information session. Details about this event can be found on the <a href=\"https:\/\/qutvirtual4.qut.edu.au\/group\/student\/orientation\/your-orientation\">your orientation<\/a> webpage.<\/p><p>This orientation session is taking place on Wednesday, we recommend having a look at other events happening during <a href=\"https:\/\/qutvirtual4.qut.edu.au\/group\/student\/student-life\/events\/welcome-week\">Welcome Week<\/a> .<\/p><p><strong>OPTIONAL:<\/strong> For those of you who&nbsp;would like to broaden your networking further \u2013 you might like to register to join in the Optional <strong>Workshop sessions from 10.15-12.15pm <\/strong>in the morning<strong>.<\/strong>&nbsp;You can find more about this on&nbsp;the <a href=\"https:\/\/qutvirtual4.qut.edu.au\/group\/student\/orientation\/your-orientation\">your orientation<\/a> webpage.<\/p>",
